$.q9=function(){var s=u.k,r=t.s,q=t.N,p=t.K,o=t.Mq,n=t.z
return A.a([A.n(["neighborhood","European Quarter","places",A.a([A.n(["id","parlement","title","European Parliament","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/bruxelles/1.jpg","assets4/belgique/bruxelles/2.jpg","assets4/belgique/bruxelles/3.jpg"],r),"history","The European Parliament is one of the major institutions of the European Union. If Brussels was chosen as its principal seat (alongside Strasbourg and Luxembourg), it is due to its central position in the heart of Europe, its historical bilingualism (French-Dutch), and its diplomatic tradition, thus avoiding favoring major historical national capitals like Paris or more out-of-the-way locations. It is the political and decision-making heart for over 450 million European citizens.","tip",s,"mapsQuery","European Parliament Brussels"],q,p),A.n(["id","cinquantenaire","title","Cinquantenaire Park","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/bruxelles/4.jpg","assets4/belgique/bruxelles/5.png"],r),"history","Created under the reign of Leopold II to celebrate the fiftieth anniversary of Belgium's independence during the national exhibition of 1880, the park is dominated by its majestic triumphal arches and major national museums (Army Museum, Autoworld). Located a stone's throw from the European Quarter, it constitutes an immense green space steeped in architectural and memorial history.","tip","Ideal in autumn and spring to enjoy the magnificent colors. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Cinquantenaire Park Brussels"],q,p),A.n(["id","leopold","title","Leopold Park","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/bruxelles/7.jpg"],r),"history","Located right behind the European Parliament (and very close to the Cinquantenaire), this historic park offers a lush green natural setting and houses unusual remains, including an authentic fragment of the Berlin Wall erected in memory of European geopolitical upheavals. Formerly Brussels' zoological garden, it testifies to the capital's urban transition.","tip","Ideal on a sunny day. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Leopold Park Brussels"],q,p)],o)],q,n),A.n(["neighborhood","Historic Center","places",A.a([A.n(["id","grandplace","title","Grand-Place","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/bruxelles/9.jpg","assets4/belgique/bruxelles/10.jpg","assets4/belgique/bruxelles/11.jpg"],r),"history","The beating historic heart of Brussels, the Grand-Place is world-renowned for the richness of its ornamental and architectural decoration, bringing together opulent guild houses, the Gothic Town Hall, and the King's House. Largely rebuilt after the destructive bombardment of 1695 by French troops, it is a UNESCO World Heritage site.","tip","A must-see both day and night. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Grand-Place Brussels"],q,p),A.n(["id","mannekenpis","title","Manneken-Pis and Jeanneke-Pis","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/bruxelles/199.jpg","assets4/belgique/bruxelles/14.jpg"],r),"history","Located in the immediate vicinity of the Grand-Place, Manneken-Pis is a small bronze fountain representing a urinating boy, symbol of the independent, defiant, and humorous spirit of the people of Brussels (dressed in traditional costumes on various occasions). Jeanneke-Pis, its female counterpart located in a neighboring alley (Impasse de la Fid\xe9lit\xe9), was created later in 1987 to promote local folklore and support charities.","tip","Plan a quick walk through the pedestrian alleys. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Manneken-Pis Brussels"],q,p),A.n(["id","galeries","title","Royal Saint-Hubert Galleries","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/bruxelles/15.jpg"],r),"history","Inaugurated in 1847 a stone's throw from the Grand-Place, these superb covered shopping galleries (divided into Gallery of the Queen, the King, and the Princes) are among the oldest and most elegant in Europe. Designed by architect Jean-Pierre Cluysenaar, they are famous for their luxury display windows, historic artisan chocolate shops, theaters, and luminous glass roof.","tip","Taste the artisan chocolates on site. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Royal Saint-Hubert Galleries Brussels"],q,p),A.n(["id","montdesarts","title","Mont des Arts","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/bruxelles/16.jpg","assets4/belgique/bruxelles/17.webp"],r),"history","Originally laid out for the 1910 International Exhibition and then completely redesigned in the 1950s during the city's major urban renewal projects, the Mont des Arts links the Upper Town (museum and royal palace district) and the Lower Town (historic center). It offers a sloping geometric garden and one of the most spectacular panoramas over the rooftops of Brussels and the Town Hall.","tip","Magnificent view at sunset. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Mont des Arts Brussels"],q,p),A.n(["id","palaisjustice","title","Palace of Justice","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/bruxelles/18.jpg","assets4/belgique/bruxelles/19.webp","assets4/belgique/bruxelles/20.webp","assets4/belgique/bruxelles/21.jpg"],r),"history","Built between 1866 and 1883 by architect Joseph Poelaert, this colossal building dominates the Marolles district and offers a breathtaking view of the city. It is one of the largest courthouse buildings constructed in 19th-century Europe, surpassing certain basilicas in its ground surface area. Its monumental architecture mixes Greco-Roman and Assyrian inspirations.","tip","Admire the sheer scale of the architecture. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Palace of Justice Brussels"],q,p)],o)],q,n),A.n(["neighborhood","Heysel / North","places",A.a([A.n(["id","atomium","title","Atomium","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/bruxelles/22.jpg","assets4/belgique/bruxelles/23.jpg","assets4/belgique/bruxelles/24.jpg"],r),"history","Designed for the 1958 Brussels World's Fair (Expo 58) by architect Andr\xe9 Waterkeyn and engineers Pol and Jean Cornellie, the Atomium represents the elementary unit of an iron crystal magnified 165 billion times. A true Belgian version of the Eiffel Tower, it symbolizes bold faith in scientific progress, modernity, and the post-war atomic era. From its summit or at its feet, one can also listen to and observe the impressive ballet of planes taking off and landing, with Zaventem airport located right next door.","tip",s,"mapsQuery","Atomium Brussels"],q,p),A.n(["id","minieurope","title","Mini-Europe","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/bruxelles/25.webp","assets4/belgique/bruxelles/26.jpg"],r),"history","Inaugurated in 1989 right at the foot of the Atomium (the two sites are thus ideally visited together), the Mini-Europe park allows visitors to tour the European Union in a few steps through nearly 350 landmark European monuments reproduced at a 1/25 scale with impressive attention to detail, animations, and sound effects.","tip",s,"mapsQuery","Mini-Europe Brussels"],q,p)],o)],q,n),A.n(["neighborhood","Laeken (North-West)","places",A.a([A.n(["id","laeken","title","Royal Greenhouses of Laeken","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/bruxelles/27.webp","assets4/belgique/bruxelles/28.jpg","assets4/belgique/bruxelles/29.webp"],r),"history","Royal residential district housing the Castle of Laeken (residence of the Belgian royal family) and its famous monumental iron and glass greenhouses. Designed by architect Alphonse Balat for King Leopold II in the late 19th century, they constitute a masterpiece of metal architecture and house rare botanical collections, open to the public only a few weeks a year in spring.","tip","Exceptional opening in spring. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Castle of Laeken Brussels"],q,p)],o)],q,n)],t._)}()
$.qa=function(){var s=t.s,r=t.N,q=t.K
return A.a([A.n(["neighborhood","Ghent Highlights","places",A.a([A.n(["id","castle_of_counts","title","The Castle of the Counts","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/gand/1.jpeg","assets4/belgique/gand/2.jpg","assets4/belgique/gand/3.jpg"],s),"history","Erected in the 12th century by Count Philip of Alsace, the Castle of the Counts (Gravensteen) is an imposing, virtually intact medieval fortress in the heart of the city. Former seat of comtal power, prison and then textile factory, it offers a captivating journey back to the time of knights and an impressive panoramic view over the rooftops of Ghent.","tip",u.k,"mapsQuery","Castle of the Counts Ghent"],r,q),A.n(["id","ghent_belfry","title","The Belfry of Ghent","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/gand/4.jpg"],s),"history","Symbol of the city's independence and communal freedoms since the 14th century, the Belfry of Ghent stands 91 meters high. Crowned by its famous gilded copper dragon watching over the city, the belfry houses a superb carillon and is part of the UNESCO World Heritage.","tip","Take the elevator to enjoy the breathtaking view without getting too exhausted. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Belfry of Ghent"],r,q),A.n(["id","saint_bavos_cathedral","title","Saint Bavo's Cathedral","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/gand/5.jpg","assets4/belgique/gand/6.jpg"],s),"history",'A harmonious blend of Romanesque, Radiant Gothic and Brabantine Gothic styles, this majestic cathedral is famous worldwide for housing one of the greatest masterpieces of Flemish painting: "The Adoration of the Mystic Lamb" by the Van Eyck brothers.',"tip","Remember to book your ticket in advance to admire the altarpiece of the Mystic Lamb. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Saint Bavo's Cathedral Ghent"],r,q),A.n(["id","graslei_korenlei","title","The Graslei and Korenlei","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/gand/7.jpg"],s),"history","Facing each other on either side of the Leie, the Graslei and the Korenlei form the historic and picturesque heart of Ghent's old merchant port. Bordered by a spectacular row of guild houses ranging from Romanesque to Renaissance style, they offer the city's finest reflections and an exceptional architectural view.","tip","The ideal place to sit on a terrace, stroll along the water at sunset or embark on a guided boat cruise. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Graslei and Korenlei Ghent"],r,q),A.n(["id","saint_michaels_bridge","title","Saint Michael's Bridge","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/gand/8.webp","assets4/belgique/gand/9.webp","assets4/belgique/gand/12.webp"],s),"history","Built of stone at the beginning of the 20th century, this iconic bridge offers the most famous and photographed viewpoint of Ghent. From its summit, one embraces a 360-degree panorama encompassing the three famous aligned towers (Saint Nicholas, the Belfry and Saint Bavo) as well as the Graslei and Korenlei quays.","tip","Especially to visit very early in the morning for photography lovers to enjoy magical light and calm. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Saint Michael's Bridge Ghent"],r,q)],t.Mq)],r,t.z)],t._)}()
$.q7=function(){var s="Antwerp-Central Station",r=t.s,q=t.N,p=t.K
return A.a([A.n(["neighborhood","Antwerp Highlights","places",A.a([A.n(["id","gare_centrale_anvers","title",s,"images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/anvers/1.jpg","assets4/belgique/anvers/2.jpg","assets4/belgique/anvers/3.webp","assets4/belgique/anvers/4.webp"],r),"history",'Often described as the "Railway Cathedral", Antwerp-Central Station is considered one of the finest railway stations in the world. Inaugurated in 1905, its monumental eclectic architecture blends a grandiose dome, a majestic marble-clad hall, and a huge iron and glass glassroof.',"tip","Take the time to admire the main hall and the glass roof from the upper levels. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery",s],q,p),A.n(["id","grote_markt_anvers","title","The Grand-Place (Grote Markt)","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/anvers/5.jpg","assets4/belgique/anvers/6.jpg","assets4/belgique/anvers/7.webp"],r),"history","The historic heart of the city, Antwerp's Grand-Place is surrounded by the majestic Italian and Flemish Renaissance-style Town Hall, as well as opulent guild houses topped with gilded statues. At its center stands the spectacular fountain representing Silvius Brabo.","tip","The perfect place to sit on a terrace and admire the illuminated facades. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Grote Markt Antwerp"],q,p),A.n(["id","cathedrale_notredame_anvers","title","The Cathedral of Our Lady","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/anvers/8.jpg"],r),"history","An absolute masterpiece of Brabantine Gothic art, the Cathedral of Our Lady of Antwerp raises its majestic bell tower to a height of 123 meters, inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage list. Its spectacular interior houses several major masterpieces by the famous baroque painter Peter Paul Rubens.","tip","Take the time to observe Rubens' monumental paintings inside. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Cathedral of Our Lady Antwerp"],q,p),A.n(["id","het_steen","title","Het Steen","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/anvers/9.webp","assets4/belgique/anvers/10.webp","assets4/belgique/anvers/12.jpg"],r),"history","Overlooking the banks of the Scheldt, Het Steen is the oldest building in the city (built in the 13th century). This former medieval fortified castle, which once served as a fortified gate and prison, now houses the visitor center and offers a panoramic terrace over the river.","tip","Go up to the rooftop terrace to enjoy an unobstructed view of the Scheldt and the port. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Het Steen Antwerp"],q,p)],t.Mq)],q,t.z)],t._)}()
$.q8=function(){var s=t.s,r=t.N,q=t.K
return A.a([A.n(["neighborhood","Bruges Highlights","places",A.a([A.n(["id","canaux_bruges","title","The Canals of Bruges","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/bruges/1.webp","assets4/belgique/bruges/2.jpg","assets4/belgique/bruges/3.webp"],s),"history",'Nicknamed the "Venice of the North", Bruges is crisscrossed by a romantic and enchanting network of canals. For many visitors, it feels like Venice only better: more intimate, verdant, and preserved. Strolling along the banks or taking a boat ride offers a magical perspective on the medieval facades.',"tip","Take a boat ride in the early morning to avoid the crowd. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Canals of Bruges"],r,q),A.n(["id","quai_rosaire","title","The Rozenhoedkaai (Quay of the Rosary)","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/bruges/4.jpg","assets4/belgique/bruges/6.jpg"],s),"history","This is the most popular and photographed spot in Bruges. With its old facades reflecting in the water and the Belfry in the background, Rozenhoedkaai brings to mind the charm of Ghent's quays (Graslei and Korenlei), while offering a landscape worthy of a postcard.","tip","A must-admire at sunset or illuminated in the evening. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Rozenhoedkaai Bruges"],r,q),A.n(["id","beffroi_bruges","title","The Belfry of Bruges","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/bruges/9.webp"],s),"history","Towering over the Market Square from its 83 meters, this iconic medieval tower once housed the city's archives, treasury, and carillon. Climbing its 366 steps offers an unforgettable panoramic view of Bruges and its surroundings.","tip","Book your ticket online in advance to avoid queues. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Belfry of Bruges"],r,q),A.n(["id","grote_markt","title","The Market Square (Grote Markt)","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/bruges/11.webp","assets4/belgique/bruges/12.webp","assets4/belgique/bruges/14.webp"],s),"history","The beating heart of the medieval city, the Grote Markt is lined with famous step-gabled houses, former cloth halls, and lively outdoor cafes. It is the ideal starting point for exploring the city on foot or by horse-drawn carriage.","tip","Enjoy the terraces at the end of the day to admire the lively square. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Grote Markt Bruges"],r,q),A.n(["id","godshuizen","title","The Godshuizen (Almshouses)","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/bruges/15.webp","assets4/belgique/bruges/16.webp"],s),"history","These small whitewashed houses, arranged around a peaceful inner courtyard, were built starting from the 14th century by wealthy citizens or guilds to house the elderly and disadvantaged. Today, they offer true havens of tranquility hidden in the heart of the city.","tip","Respect the absolute calm of these inhabited inner courtyards. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Godshuizen Bruges"],r,q),A.n(["id","moulins_bruges","title","The Windmills of Bruges","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/bruges/17.jpeg"],s),"history","Located on the old green ramparts to the north-east of the city (Kruisvest), these impressive wooden windmills recall the era when they ground grain for the city. The Sint-Janshuis mill is one of the few still operating in its original location.","tip","Ideal for a lovely walk or bike ride along the canal. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Windmills Kruisvest Bruges"],r,q),A.n(["id","basilique_saintsang","title","The Basilica of the Holy Blood","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/bruges/20.jpg","assets4/belgique/bruges/21.webp"],s),"history","Located on Burg Square, this basilica consists of two superimposed chapels: a Romanesque lower chapel dedicated to Saint Basil and a Gothic upper chapel housing the relic of the Holy Blood, brought back from the Holy Land during the Second Crusade.","tip","Discover the two chapels with their highly contrasting architectural styles. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Basilica of the Holy Blood Bruges"],r,q)],t.Mq)],r,t.z)],t._)}()
$.qi=function(){var s=t.s,r=t.N,q=t.K
return A.a([A.n(["neighborhood","Liege Highlights","places",A.a([A.n(["id","montagne_de_bueren","title","The Montagne de Bueren","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/liege/1.webp","assets4/belgique/liege/2.webp","assets4/belgique/liege/1 bis.webp"],s),"history","A famous 374-step monumental staircase built in the 19th century, the Montagne de Bueren offers one of Belgium's most picturesque urban challenges. Its summit reveals a breathtaking and unforgettable panorama over the Burning City and the Meuse.","tip","Take your time climbing the steps and admire the view at the summit. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Montagne de Bueren Liege"],r,q),A.n(["id","citadel_hillsides","title","The Citadel Hillsides","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/liege/3.jpg","assets4/belgique/liege/4.jpg"],s),"history","A true green lung suspended above the city center, the Hillsides bring together nearly 90 listed monuments, steep paths, old orchards, and historical terraces. A haven of charm and tranquility just a stone's throw from the city.","tip","Wear comfortable shoes to navigate the cobblestone paths and trails. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Citadel Hillsides Liege"],r,q),A.n(["id","liege_guillemins_station","title","Liege-Guillemins Station","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/liege/5.jpg","assets4/belgique/liege/6.webp","assets4/belgique/liege/7.jpg"],s),"history","Designed by renowned Spanish architect Santiago Calatrava, this monumental and futuristic station surprises with its immense self-supporting steel and glass vault. It perfectly embodies the renewal and modern dynamism of the city.","tip","Admire the magnificent plays of light through the glass roof at different times of the day. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Liege-Guillemins Railway Station"],r,q),A.n(["id","saint_pauls_cathedral","title","Saint Paul's Cathedral","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/liege/8.jpg"],s),"history","The spiritual heart of the city, Saint Paul's Cathedral elegantly marries Gothic and Rayonnant Gothic styles. It houses magnificent mural paintings, spectacular stained glass windows, and a remarkable treasury of religious goldsmithing.","tip","Enjoy the calm of the adjoining cloister for a serene break in the heart of the center. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Saint Paul's Cathedral Liege"],r,q),A.n(["id","old_town_lanes","title","The Alleys and Dead Ends of Liege","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/liege/10.jpg","assets4/belgique/liege/15.jpg","assets4/belgique/liege/12.webp"],s),"history","Far from preconceived notions, Liege is full of hidden treasures like the Hors-Ch\xe2teau district and the Cour Saint-Antoine. These cobblestone alleys, lined with restored old houses and greenery, reveal an unappreciated poetic and romantic charm.","tip","Venturing into Impasse de l'Ange or Couronne for an authentic experience. Check the weather before leaving.","mapsQuery","Hors-Chateau District Liege"],r,q)],t.Mq)],r,t.z)],t._)}()
$.qg=function(){var s=t.s,r=t.N,q=t.K
return A.a([A.n(["quartier","Les Incontournables de Gand","lieux",A.a([A.n(["id","chateau_comtes","titre","Le Ch\xe2teau des Comtes","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/gand/1.jpeg","assets4/belgique/gand/2.jpg","assets4/belgique/gand/3.jpg"],s),"histoire","\xc9rig\xe9 au XIIe si\xe8cle par le comte Philippe d'Alsace, le Ch\xe2teau des Comtes (Gravensteen) est une imposante forteresse m\xe9di\xe9vale pratiquement intacte au c\u0153ur de la ville. Ancien si\xe8ge du pouvoir comtal, prison puis usine textile, il offre un voyage captivant au temps des chevaliers et une vue panoramique impressionnante sur les toits de Gand.","conseil",u.D,"mapsQuery","Ch\xe2teau des Comtes Gand"],r,q),A.n(["id","beffroi_gand","titre","Le Beffroi de Gand","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/gand/4.jpg"],s),"histoire","Symbole de l'ind\xe9pendance et des libert\xe9s communales de la ville depuis le XIVe si\xe8cle, le Beffroi de Gand s'\xe9l\xe8ve \xe0 91 m\xe8tres de hauteur. Couronn\xe9 par son c\xe9l\xe8bre dragon en cuivre dor\xe9 qui veille sur la cit\xe9, le beffroi abrite un superbe carillon et fait partie du patrimoine mondial de l'UNESCO.","conseil","Prendre l'ascenseur pour profiter de la vue imprenable sans trop s'\xe9puiser. V\xe9rifier la m\xe9t\xe9o avant de partir.","mapsQuery","Beffroi de Gand"],r,q),A.n(["id","saint_bavon","titre","La Cath\xe9drale Saint-Bavon","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/gand/5.jpg","assets4/belgique/gand/6.jpg"],s),"histoire","M\xe9lange harmonieux de styles roman, gothique rayonnant et gothique braban\xe7on, cette majestueuse cath\xe9drale est c\xe9l\xe8bre dans le monde entier pour abriter l'un des plus grands chefs-d'\u0153uvre de la peinture flamande : \"L'Adoration de l'Agneau mystique\" des fr\xe8res Van Eyck.","conseil","Penser \xe0 r\xe9server votre billet \xe0 l'avance pour admirer le retable de l'Agneau Mystique. V\xe9rifier la m\xe9t\xe9o avant de partir.","mapsQuery","Cath\xe9drale Saint-Bavon Gand"],r,q),A.n(["id","quai_herbes_grains","titre",u.u,"images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/gand/7.jpg"],s),"histoire","Face \xe0 face de chaque c\xf4t\xe9 de la Lys, le Quai aux Herbes (Graslei) et le Quai aux Grains (Korenlei) forment le c\u0153ur historique et pittoresque du vieux port marchand de Gand. Bord\xe9s par une rang\xe9e spectaculaire de maisons de corporations allant du style roman \xe0 la Renaissance, ils offrent les plus beaux reflets de la ville et une vue architecturale d'exception.","conseil","L'endroit id\xe9al pour s'installer en terrasse, se promener au bord de l'eau au coucher du soleil ou embarquer \xe0 bord d'une croisi\xe8re guid\xe9e en bateau. V\xe9rifier la m\xe9t\xe9o avant de partir.","mapsQuery","Graslei et Korenlei Gand"],r,q),A.n(["id","pont_saint_michel","titre","Le Pont Saint-Michel","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/gand/8.webp","assets4/belgique/gand/9.webp","assets4/belgique/gand/12.webp"],s),"histoire","Construit en pierre au d\xe9but du XXe si\xe8cle, ce pont embl\xe9matique offre le point de vue le plus c\xe9l\xe8bre et photographi\xe9 de Gand. Depuis son sommet, on embrasse un panorama \xe0 360 degr\xe9s englobant les trois c\xe9l\xe8bres tours align\xe9es (Saint-Nicolas, le Beffroi et Saint-Bavon) ainsi que les quais Graslei et Korenlei.","conseil","Surtout \xe0 visiter tr\xe8s t\xf4t le matin pour les amateurs de photographie afin de profiter d'une lumi\xe8re magique et du calme. V\xe9rifier la m\xe9t\xe9o avant de partir.","mapsQuery","Pont Saint-Michel Gand"],r,q)],t.Mq)],r,t.z)],t._)}()
$.qd=function(){var s=t.s,r=t.N,q=t.K
return A.a([A.n(["quartier","Les Incontournables d'Anvers","lieux",A.a([A.n(["id","gare_centrale_anvers","titre","La Gare d'Anvers-Central","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/anvers/1.jpg","assets4/belgique/anvers/2.jpg","assets4/belgique/anvers/3.webp","assets4/belgique/anvers/4.webp"],s),"histoire","Souvent qualifi\xe9e de \"Cath\xe9drale du Rail\", la Gare d'Anvers-Central est consid\xe9r\xe9e comme l'une des plus belles gares ferroviaires au monde. Inaugur\xe9e en 1905, son architecture \xe9clectique monumentale m\xeale un d\xf4me grandiose, un hall majestueux rev\xeatu de marbre et une immense verri\xe8re en fer et en verre.","conseil","Prendre le temps d'admirer le hall principal et la verri\xe8re depuis les niveaux sup\xe9rieurs. V\xe9rifier la m\xe9t\xe9o avant de partir.","mapsQuery","Gare d'Anvers-Central"],r,q),A.n(["id","grote_markt_anvers","titre","La Grand-Place (Grote Markt)","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/anvers/5.jpg","assets4/belgique/anvers/6.jpg","assets4/belgique/anvers/7.webp"],s),"histoire","C\u0153ur historique de la ville, la Grand-Place d'Anvers est entour\xe9e par le majestueux H\xf4tel de Ville de style Renaissance italienne et flamande, ainsi que par d'opulentes maisons de corporations surmont\xe9es de statues dor\xe9es. En son centre se dresse la fontaine spectaculaire repr\xe9sentant Silvius Brabo.","conseil","L'endroit parfait pour s'installer en terrasse et admirer les fa\xe7ades illumin\xe9es. V\xe9rifier la m\xe9t\xe9o avant de partir.","mapsQuery","Grote Markt Anvers"],r,q),A.n(["id","cathedrale_notredame_anvers","titre","La Cath\xe9drale Notre-Dame","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/anvers/8.jpg"],s),"histoire","Chef-d'\u0153uvre absolu de l'art gothique braban\xe7on, la cath\xe9drale Notre-Dame d'Anvers dresse son clocher majestueux \xe0 123 m\xe8tres de hauteur, inscrit au patrimoine mondial de l'UNESCO. Son int\xe9rieur spectaculaire abrite plusieurs chefs-d'\u0153uvre majeurs du c\xe9l\xe8bre peintre baroque Pierre Paul Rubens.","conseil","Prendre le temps d'observer les tableaux monumentaux de Rubens \xe0 l'int\xe9rieur. V\xe9rifier la m\xe9t\xe9o avant de partir.","mapsQuery","Cath\xe9drale Notre-Dame Anvers"],r,q),A.n(["id","het_steen","titre","Le Het Steen","images",A.a(["assets4/belgique/anvers/9.webp","assets4/belgique/anvers/10.webp","assets4/belgique/anvers/11.webp"],s),"histoire","Surveillant les berges de l'Escaut, le Het Steen est le plus ancien b\xe2timent de la ville (\xe9rig\xe9 au XIIIe si\xe8cle). Cet ancien ch\xe2teau fort m\xe9di\xe9val, qui servait autrefois de porte fortifi\xe9e et de prison, accueille d\xe9sormais le centre d'accueil des visiteurs et offre une terrasse panoramique sur le fleuve.","conseil","Monter sur le toit-terrasse pour b\xe9n\xe9ficier d'une vue d\xe9gag\xe9e sur l'Escaut et le port. V\xe9rifier la m\xe9t\xe9o avant de partir.","mapsQuery","Het Steen Anvers"],r,q)],t.Mq)],r,t.z)],t._)}()
